  "evidences": [
    {
      "id": "ev_4",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s4"
      },
      "text": "Payloads from the exploit may include Backdoor.Emdivi , Backdoor.Korplug , and Backdoor.ZXshell ; however, all payloads aim to steal confidential information from the compromised computer.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_5",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s5"
      },
      "text": "The content of the emails vary depending on the business interest of the targeted recipient’s organization; however, all are about recent political events associated with Japan.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_8",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s8"
      },
      "text": "However, during our investigation of this Ichitaro zero-day attack, we discovered that the attack was in fact part of an ongoing cyberespionage campaign specifically targeting various Japanese organizations.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_24",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s4"
      },
      "text": "Payload The malicious payload is Backdoor.Emdivi, a threat that opens a back door on the compromised computer.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_25",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s5"
      },
      "text": "The malware is exclusively used in the CloudyOmega attack campaign and first appeared in 2011 when it was used in an attack against a Japanese chemical company.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_28",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s8"
      },
      "text": "Allow a remote attacker to execute code through HTTP Steal credentials stored by Internet Explorer Type T is primarily used in Operation CloudyOmega, has been in constant development since the campaign was first launched in 2011, and is written in the C++ programing language.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_29",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s9"
      },
      "text": "Type T employs techniques to protect itself from security vendors or network administrators.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_30",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s1"
      },
      "text": "VirtualMachine Debugger Sandbox Type S, on the other hand, was used only twice in the attack campaign.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_31",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s2"
      },
      "text": "Type S is a .NET application based on the same source code and shared C&C infrastructure as Type T.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_32",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s3"
      },
      "text": "One interesting trait of Type S is that it uses Japanese sentences that seem to be randomly taken from the internet to change the file hash.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_35",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s6"
      },
      "text": "We discovered that 40 out of the 50 compromised websites, spread across 13 IP addresses, are hosted on a single cloud-hosting service based in Japan.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_38",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s3"
      },
      "text": "System Infected: Backdoor.Emdivi Activity System Infected: Backdoor.Emdivi Activity 2 Zero-day and links to other cybercriminal groups",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_40",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s5"
      },
      "text": "In August 2012, the CloudyOmega attackers exploited the zero-day Adobe Flash Player and AIR 'copyRawDataTo()' Integer Overflow Vulnerability (CVE-2012-5054) in an attack against a high-profile organization in Japan.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_42",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s7"
      },
      "text": "Once successfully exploited, the file installed Backdoor.Emdivi.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_46",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s11"
      },
      "text": "The Flash file seems to have been created using the same framework used by the CloudyOmega group, but with a different exploit.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_53",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_CloudyOmega_Ichitaro",
      "locator": {
        "page": 7,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p7_s1"
      },
      "text": "Conclusion Operation CloudyOmega was launched by an attack group that has communication channels with other notorious attack groups including Hidden Lynx and the group responsible for LadyBoyle.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
